{"source_id":"src-0021","title":"thumbmarkjs browser fingerprinting library","publisher":"thumbmarkjs","url":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@thumbmarkjs/thumbmarkjs","source_type":"open_source_package","authority":"tier1","publication_date":"2026-09-25","accessed_at":"2026-10-06","topics":["device_signals","license","maintenance"],"scope":{"domain":"browser device signal collection","package":"@thumbmarkjs/thumbmarkjs"},"acquisition_method":"npm_registry","license":"MIT","attribution_required":false,"update_terms":"npm releases; v1.12.0 last modified 2026-09-25","boundary":"supports: the package is mit licensed and was published within two weeks of access. the 1.12.0 tarball was read (dist bundle and type declarations): it has thirteen components, including permissions (camera, microphone and geolocation permission states), locales (timezone and language) and speech (installed voice list); by default it samples telemetry to api.thumbmarkjs.com and may fetch a script from experimental.thumbmarkjs.com, which the logging option disables; a collect beacon needs an api key. its webrtc component uses an empty ice server list and reads codec and extension lines only, so no ip address was found in that version. does not support: any other version, fingerprint accuracy claims, or a guarantee that a later release keeps these properties. re-verify on upgrade."}
{"source_id":"src-0022","title":"GeoLite End User License Agreement","publisher":"MaxMind","url":"https://www.maxmind.com/en/geolite2/eula","source_type":"vendor_license_terms","authority":"tier1","publication_date":"2026-02-12","accessed_at":"2026-10-06","topics":["ip_intelligence","geo","license"],"scope":{"domain":"ip geolocation database terms","product":"GeoLite2"},"acquisition_method":"firecrawl","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0 plus the maxmind geolite eula","attribution_required":true,"update_terms":"use updated databases promptly; destroy old versions within 30 days of a new release","boundary":"supports: country and subdivision geo lookups under these terms, the attribution requirement, and the update and destroy obligation. does not support: any vpn, proxy or anonymizer claim, redistribution of database files from this repo, or a legal reading of the share-alike clause for derived data (not reviewed)."}
{"source_id":"src-0023","title":"IP2Proxy LITE PX2 database and data license","publisher":"IP2Location","url":"https://lite.ip2location.com/database/px2-ip-proxytype-country","source_type":"vendor_license_terms","authority":"tier1","publication_date":null,"accessed_at":"2026-10-06","topics":["ip_intelligence","proxy","license"],"scope":{"domain":"open proxy database","product":"IP2Proxy LITE PX2","license_url":"https://lite.ip2location.com/data-license"},"acquisition_method":"firecrawl","license":"free of charge under the ip2location lite terms of use; attribution acknowledgment required","attribution_required":true,"update_terms":"cadence stated inconsistently: the product page says bi-weekly, the database page shows a monthly next-update date","boundary":"supports: open proxies (pub) with country and proxy type. does not support: vpn, tor exit, datacenter or hosting, residential proxy detection (commercial edition only), accuracy claims, or ipv6 parity claims. license caveats: clause 2 forbids redistributing or reselling the product while clause 5 permits distribution with credit, and clause 4 is absent from the published numbering. not legally reviewed. this repo never commits the database. the acknowledgment wording on the data license page names ip2location geolocation, so the exact ip2proxy wording needs confirming before launch."}
{"source_id":"src-0024","title":"VPN and datacenter IP lists","publisher":"X4BNet","url":"https://github.com/X4BNet/lists_vpn","source_type":"community_dataset","authority":"tier3","publication_date":null,"accessed_at":"2026-10-06","topics":["ip_intelligence","vpn","datacenter","license"],"scope":{"domain":"ipv4 vpn and datacenter netblocks","paths":["output/vpn/ipv4.txt","output/datacenter/ipv4.txt"]},"acquisition_method":"firecrawl","license":"MIT (license text appears in the readme; no separate LICENSE file at the main branch root)","attribution_required":true,"update_terms":"rebuilt by github actions from source asn data; latest commit 2026-10-05 at access","boundary":"supports: ipv4 known vpn netblocks and ipv4 datacenter or non-eyeball ranges, largely derived from asns. does not support: ipv6, completeness (the readme says not all vpns are listed), per-provider accuracy, or residential proxies. the datacenter list is a superset that includes vpns, so a vpn hit also implies a datacenter hit. the legacy ipv4.txt path is slated for removal in 2026 and is not used."}
{"source_id":"src-0025","title":"Tor bulk exit list","publisher":"The Tor Project","url":"https://check.torproject.org/torbulkexitlist","source_type":"project_published_list","authority":"tier2","publication_date":null,"accessed_at":"2026-10-06","topics":["ip_intelligence","tor","license"],"scope":{"domain":"ipv4 tor exit relay addresses"},"acquisition_method":"http_get","license":"no explicit license statement found on the list, the tor metrics collector page, or the tor metrics about page","attribution_required":false,"update_terms":"live list; 19348 ipv4 entries and no ipv6 entries at access","boundary":"supports: ipv4 addresses listed as tor exit relays at fetch time. does not support: ipv6 exits, bridges or non-exit relays, historical membership, or any license grant. the missing license statement is recorded as a gap and is not assumed to be permissive."}
{"source_id":"src-0026","title":"maxmind npm package (mmdb reader)","publisher":"runk (Dmitry Shirokov)","url":"https://github.com/runk/node-maxmind","source_type":"open_source_package","authority":"tier1","publication_date":null,"accessed_at":"2026-10-06","topics":["ip_intelligence","geo"],"scope":{"domain":"geolite2/geoip2 mmdb binary format reader","package":"maxmind@5.0.7","transitive_dependencies":["mmdb-lib@3.0.3 (mit)","tiny-lru@13.0.0 (bsd-3-clause)"]},"acquisition_method":"npm_registry","license":"MIT","attribution_required":false,"update_terms":"npm releases; pinned exact at 5.0.7 in package.json, no automatic update","boundary":"supports: reading a geolite2/geoip2 country or city mmdb file and returning country.iso_code, registered_country.iso_code, and subdivisions[].iso_code; a miss (no record for an address, including anonymous networks and satellite ranges) returns null, not an error. does not support: any claim about geolite2 data accuracy or coverage, which is governed separately by src-0022. the library itself contains no provider data; this repo never commits an .mmdb file."}
